#. type: Plain text
#: content/module-reference/processing-modules/invert.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"color of film material\n"
": Clicking on the colored field will open a color selector dialog which offers you a choice of commonly used colors, or allows you to define an RGB color. You can also activate the [picker](../../darkroom/processing-modules/module-controls.md#pickers) to take a color probe from your image – preferably from the unexposed border of your negative.\n"
msgstr ""
"color of film material\n"
": ການຄລິກໃສ່ຊ່ອງສີຈະເປັນການເປີດໜ້າຕ່າງເລືອກສີ ເພື່ອໃຫ້ທ່ານເລືອກສີທີ່ນິຍົມໃຊ້ທົ່ວໄປ ຫຼື ກຳນົດສີ RGB ດ້ວຍຕົນ"
"ເອງ. ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດເປີດໃຊ້ [ເຄື່ອງມືດູດສີ](../../darkroom/processing-modules/module-"
"controls.md#pickers) ເພື່ອສຸ່ມຕົວຢ່າງສີຈາກຮູບພາບຂອງທ່ານ – ໂດຍປົກກະຕິແມ່ນເລືອກຈາກຂອບຟີມສ່ວນທີ່ບໍ່"
"ໄດ້ຮັບແສງ.\n"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/module-reference/processing-modules/filmic-rgb.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "filmic rgb"
msgstr "ຟິລມິກ RGB (filmic rgb)"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/module-reference/processing-modules/filmic-rgb.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"description\n"
": apply a view transform to prepare the scene-referred pipeline for display on SDR screens and paper prints while preventing clipping in non-destructive ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"ລາຍລະອຽດ\n"
": ນຳໃຊ້ການແປງມຸມມອງເພື່ອຈັດກຽມ pipeline ແບບ scene-referred ສຳລັບການສະແດງຜົນເທິງຈໍ SDR ແລະ ການພິມເທິງເຈ້ຍ ພ້ອມທັງປ້ອງກັນແສງລົ້ນ (clipping) ດ້ວຍວິທີທີ່ບໍ່ທຳລາຍຂໍ້ມູນຕົ້ນສະບັບ.\n"

